  "lead_raw_text": " The orthorhombic Ca8Ge4C4 phase (reduced formula Ca2GeC) crystallizes in space group Amm2 (No. 38), with 16 atoms per unit cell distributed over five independent Wyckoff orbits. Geometry-derived analysis shows carbon centers coordinated by two Ca neighbors at 2.3823 Å, while Ca environments include tetrahedral motifs with one C and three Ge neighbors, and Ca centers with four C neighbors. Germanium centers display four- and six-neighbor coordination to Ca, the latter described as octahedral. Validated polyhedron-sharing analysis identifies corner- and edge-sharing between Ca tetrahedra, and corner-, edge-, and face-sharing among Ca 4-vertex polyhedra, forming a three-dimensional geometric neighbor network.\n<CRYSTAL_START>",
